= Module 4: Constructive Work & Simon Boycott (1923–1929)

== 4.1 Swarajists vs. No-Changers
Following the suspension, Congress divided into two tactical camps at the 1922 Gaya Session:
- *Swarajists (Pro-Changers):* *C.R. Das* and *Motilal Nehru* founded the *Congress-Khilafat Swarajya Party* (Jan 1923) to enter legislative councils and wreck colonial governance from within. In 1925, *Vithalbhai Patel* was elected Speaker of the Central Legislative Assembly.
- *No-Changers:* *C. Rajagopalachari*, *Vallabhbhai Patel*, and *Rajendra Prasad* advocated dedicating all energy to rural constructive work.

Gandhi harmonized both factions in 1924, allowing council entry while he led rural revitalization through the *All-India Spinners' Association* (1925), Harijan upliftment, and national education.

== 4.2 Simon Commission and Nehru Report (1927–1928)
- *Simon Commission:* Appointed in Nov 1927 under *Sir John Simon* to evaluate constitutional progress; all seven members were British. Greeted on 3 Feb 1928 with nationwide strikes and chants of *"Simon Go Back!"* On 30 Oct 1928 in Lahore, *Lala Lajpat Rai* was brutally lathi-charged and died on 17 Nov 1928, declaring: *"Every blow on my back is a nail in the coffin of the British Empire."*
- *Nehru Report (1928):* Drafted by an All-Parties committee under *Motilal Nehru*; demanded *Dominion Status*, joint electorates with minority seat reservation, fundamental rights, and adult suffrage. Rejected by Jinnah (who issued his *14 Points*) and opposed by young radicals (Jawaharlal Nehru, Subhas Chandra Bose) who demanded complete independence.

== 4.3 The Lahore Congress: Purna Swaraj (1929)
In December 1929, under the presidency of *Jawaharlal Nehru*, the Congress held its historic session on the banks of the Ravi at Lahore:
1. Passed the resolution declaring *Purna Swaraj* (Complete Independence) as the national objective.
2. Authorized Gandhi to launch the Civil Disobedience Movement.
3. Hoisted the tricolor flag at midnight on *31 December 1929*.
4. Fixed *26 January 1930* as the first *Purna Swaraj Day* (Independence Day).

