= Module 5: Civil Disobedience Movement & RTC Negotiations (1930–1934)

== 5.1 The Salt Satyagraha & Dandi March (1930)
After Viceroy Irwin rejected Gandhi's *Eleven Demands* (including abolition of the salt tax and 50% land revenue cut), Gandhi selected the *Salt Law* as the catalyst of rebellion. Salt was an indispensable necessity for all classes, and the state monopoly heavily taxed the poor while preventing natural collection along India's coasts.

- *The March:* On *12 March 1930*, Gandhi and *78 ashramites* departed Sabarmati Ashram, marching *240 miles* across Gujarat in 24 days.
- *The Invalidation:* On *6 April 1930*, Gandhi collected a handful of salt from the Dandi shore, declaring: *"With this, I am shaking the foundations of the British Empire."*

